{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:8e4a1d220c1ee1a0","name":"Phase 0 Dark Trooper","source":{"id":"source:reference-8e4a1d220c1ee1a0","title":"Phase 0 Dark Trooper","revision":24494,"timestamp":"2024-11-03T15:35:25Z","sha256":"cb4e73c5af2b85682e721f1cdedcdf120a5f4073c0fafd67a1be3a96dc421cdd","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24494","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Phase%200%20Dark%20Trooper&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-8e4a1d220c1ee1a0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Faced with an increasing shortage of experienced troops, the Empire went to great lengths to supplement its forces. In addition to the introduction of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spaarti Stormtroopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spaarti_Stormtroopers"}," and the continued training of new recruits, the Empire began implementing a gruesome program that kept veterans of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," in the fight- at least for a little while. A secret project, codenamed Dark Trooper Phase Zero, involved taking aging Clone Troopers and replacing their limbs and many internal organs with cybernetic replacements. Based out of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Empirical"]},", a hidden space station in the Dominus Sector, the Dark Trooper Phase Zero project was overseen by a young Imperial officer by the name of Lt. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rom Mohc"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rom_Mohc?action=edit&redlink=1"},". Much of the same technology that was used to transform ",{"tag":"a","children":["Anakin Skywalker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Anakin_Skywalker","referenceId":"reference:e7c68f75d23b428e"}," into the cyborg ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Vader"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Vader","referenceId":"reference:c167be702b56cffc"}," found its way into the Dark Trooper Phase Zero project, and with moderate success. With their aging limbs and organs replaced by cybernetic parts, these Clone Troopers could benefit from their combat training and experience while their cybernetic limbs remained in peak condition, not suffering the effects of the clones' advanced aging.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though none can argue that the Dark Trooper Phase Zero project managed to do what it set out to accomplish, it would be less than accurate to call the project a success. Many of these cybernetically enhanced Clone Troopers were chosen for the project against their will, and they found themselves turned into soldiers who were more machine than man. Many Phase 0 Dark Troopers considered themselves monstrous abominations and attempted suicide rather than live as something less than ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},". In some cases the project replaced over 70% of a clone's body with mechanical parts, yet another in a long line of experiments that disregarded the humanity of the Clone Troopers.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Despite these drawbacks and the gruesome nature of the experiment, a significant number of Phase 0 Dark Troopers made their way onto the battlefield and were undeniably effective, combining the experience and  training of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Veteran Clone Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Veteran_Clone_Troopers"}," with the superior physical attributes of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cyborg Hybrid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cyborg_Hybrid","referenceId":"reference:ae8b2015bca59844"},". As the Empire increases in power, and recruiting techniques make up for the loss of Clone Troopers, the Dark Trooper Phase Zero project declines and is eventually shut down. However, the effectiveness of these cybernetically enhanced troops would lead Lt. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rom Mohc"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rom_Mohc?action=edit&redlink=1"},", who would eventually become a general, to convince the Emperor to reinstate the Dark Trooper project and create mechanical troops to fight the Rebellion that could operate without fear of death, aging, illness, or any other weaknesses of the flesh.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Phase 0 Dark Trooper Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Cyborg Hybrid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cyborg_Hybrid","referenceId":"reference:ae8b2015bca59844"},") ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{